      "url": "https://github.com/TFourniax/tooltest-2/pull/11#discussion_r4051821830",
      "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Exclude local and platform imports from dependencies**\n\nWhen the JS/TS provider returns textual targets such as `./local.js` or `node:fs` (or Rust returns `std::...`), this branch copies them directly, unlike the legacy extractor that filters relative, Node built-in, and Rust standard-library imports. Because `inferFileRole` treats any dependency as evidence of an external integration and the package explanation describes dependencies as third-party code, projects using only local or platform imports receive false integration and supply-chain claims whenever the optional grammars are installed. Apply the same external-dependency filtering to canonical targets.\n\nUseful? React with \ud83d\udc4d\u00a0/ \ud83d\udc4e.",
